   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Cleary played guitar on this song while Krasno switched over to bass [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **One in 7**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **What You See Is What You Get**: back after 44 archived shows (749 days); rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Something�s Got A Hold on Me (Cleary)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Motherless Child**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Walk With Me (duo/Sco/Cleary)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Don�t Need No Doctor (Cleary on guitar/ Krasno on bass)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Hottentot**: back after 43 archived shows (748 days); rare: 12 archived performances [2]\n- **enc break**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2014-03-18.140s.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 14 songs; 194 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The Tuesday night show was packed; two fans, Fernanda and Redbone, blocked holes in the crowd [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2014-03-18.140s.flac16**: taped by Frank D'Auria; transferred by Frank D'Auria; source: Neumann SKM140's>Edirol R44 [1]. Also: Transfer chain ran Audacity, then CD Wave Editor, then TLH; mastered and uploaded by Frank D'Auria [1]",
